# Enterprise Python Automation Capstone Project

A command-line automation tool that reads transaction-style CSV data, calculates summary statistics, and creates a formatted PDF report. It can also repeat report generation on a configurable interval.

## Features
- CSV input validation and useful error messages
- Summary metrics: record count, total, average, and totals by category
- PDF output with executive summary, category totals, and transaction details
- CLI commands built with `argparse`
- Repeating scheduler loop
- Logging and unit tests with `pytest`

## Requirements
- Python 3.10+
- pip

## Setup (Windows PowerShell)
```powershell
# Open a terminal in the project folder
py -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

If PowerShell blocks activation, use Command Prompt instead:
```bat
.venv\Scripts\activate.bat
```

## Generate a report
```powershell
report-automation report --input data/sample_data.csv --output output/sales_report.pdf
```

Alternative without installing the CLI entry point:
```powershell
python -m report_automation.cli report --input data/sample_data.csv --output output/sales_report.pdf
```

## Run the scheduler
Creates a new timestamped PDF every 60 minutes by default. Stop with `Ctrl+C`.
```powershell
python -m report_automation.cli schedule --input data/sample_data.csv --output-dir output --interval 60
```
For a quick test, use `--interval 1`.

## Run tests
```powershell
python -m pytest -v
```

## CSV format
The input CSV must have these columns:
- `date` — transaction date or label
- `category` — grouping/category name
- `amount` — numeric amount

A sample file is included at `data/sample_data.csv`.

## Project structure
```text
enterprise_python_automation/
├── data/
│   └── sample_data.csv
├── report_automation/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── cli.py
│   └── report.py
├── tests/
│   └── test_report.py
├── output/                 # generated PDFs are saved here
├── pyproject.toml
└── README.md
```

## Architecture
```text
CSV input
   |
   v
CSV validation --> Summary calculations
                         |
                         v
                   PDF report builder
                         |
                         v
                    Output PDF

CLI (argparse) controls one-time reports or scheduled repeats.
```

## Evidence for mentor review
1. Push the complete repository to GitHub.
2. Run one report and include a screenshot of the terminal plus the generated PDF.
3. Run `python -m pytest -v` and capture the passing test output.
4. Submit the GitHub repository link and a short screen-recorded walkthrough if requested.

## Limitations
The scheduler runs only while the process is running. For unattended production scheduling, use Windows Task Scheduler, cron, or a managed job scheduler. Sample data is fictional.
